## 3 · Implementation
Here is a deliberately small Java sketch. Apply the check before loading or returning ticket content, and repeat authorization for updates and downloads. Use authenticated server-side identities, not a user ID submitted in a request.

```java
boolean canRead(Ticket ticket, Principal actor) {
    return ticket.customerId().equals(actor.id())
        || (actor.isAgent() && actor.id().equals(ticket.assignedAgentId()));
}
```

This is **illustrative code**, not a complete security implementation. Supervisor access remains an open requirement. Avoid distinguishing “ticket exists but access denied” from “ticket absent” in customer-facing responses when that would expose another customer's activity.

The download is a review checklist. Nothing has been written to a project folder.
